  "summary_en": "Kentucky HB 7 (Acts Ch. 176, 2024) establishes a regulatory framework for fully autonomous vehicles on public highways, including insurance, registration, law enforcement interaction plans, operator definition, a human driver requirement for heavy trucks until 2026, and state preemption of local regulation. The page shows legislative history, including veto override.",
